  {
   "id": "typical",
   "title": "Application circuit with an MCU on I2C",
   "page": 15,
   "description": "The sensor U1 sits on a microcontroller's I2C bus. VDD comes straight from the supply with a 1 µF ceramic capacitor from VDD to GND placed close to the pin. SCL, SDA and the open-drain INT each run directly to the matching MCU pin and each has its own pull-up (RSCL, RSDA, RINT) to the bus pull-up supply; 10 kΩ is the typical value, and the I2C specification sets the limits for the bus pull-ups. INT is a wired-AND line like SDA and SCL.",
